        <mxCell id="note_creds" value="&lt;b&gt;Credentials&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Each role's password is a Kubernetes Secret rendered by External Secrets from OpenBao KV (secret/local/databases/&amp;lt;cluster&amp;gt;/&amp;lt;service&amp;gt;) and reloaded by CNPG. notification is the exception: its password is owned by the OpenBao database engine, which rotates it every 720 h, and External Secrets reads database/static-creds/notification every minute. PgDog takes the product-db role secrets through its HelmRelease valuesFrom; backups authenticate to RustFS with pg-backup-rustfs-credentials." style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=11;fontColor=#475569;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="990" width="1280" height="60" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="note_dr" value="&lt;b&gt;Why the DR replica reads from RustFS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;product-db-replica never connects to the primary: it bootstraps from product-db's base backup and then replays its WAL archive from the bucket, so it survives the loss of the product-db pods. Its designated primary keeps its own archive and a daily backup in product-db-replica/ (7 d). Migrations always target the -rw service directly, never a pooler." style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=11;fontColor=#475569;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="1062" width="1280" height="60" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
